<title>FRANCE: Europe Council passes bioethics convention.</title>
<headline>Europe Council passes bioethics convention.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG, France 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Council of Europe on Tuesday passed what it said was the first international convention on bioethics, intended to prevent abuse of medical, biological and genetic techniques.</p>
<p>It took the human rights watchdog five years to draft the convention which bans using the human body, or body parts, for profit.</p>
<p>It says tests to detect genetic diseases may only be carried out for medical purposes or medical research. Intervention on genes may only be undertaken to prevent, diagnose or cure genetic diseases.</p>
</text>
